<item><title>Niger and Algeria advance technical work on trans-Saharan gas pipeline</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/ne/niger-and-algeria-advance-technical-work-on-trans-saharan-6777e0/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/ne/niger-and-algeria-advance-technical-work-on-trans-saharan-6777e0/</guid><category>Niger</category><description>An Algerian delegation is in Niamey from 17 to 20 November to settle route studies and operational steps for the Nigeria-to-Algeria project.</description><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 09:03:01 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ne.jpg" length="31036" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ne.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Niger investment agency visits three firms receiving tax-code benefits</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/ne/niger-investment-agency-visits-three-firms-receiving-tax-bd17b8/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/ne/niger-investment-agency-visits-three-firms-receiving-tax-bd17b8/</guid><category>Niger</category><description>The Niamey delegation reviewed production and jobs at Murex, Nataro Agro and Bénie, which benefit from the investment code.</description><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 19:06:31 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ne.jpg" length="31036" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ne.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Tillabéri handball league launches four-day tournament with five teams</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/ne/tillaberi-handball-league-launches-four-day-tournament-with-6fbd61/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/ne/tillaberi-handball-league-launches-four-day-tournament-with-6fbd61/</guid><category>Niger</category><description>The regional league opened the competition on 16 November, with the youth council president linking its peace theme to insecurity in the region.</description><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 17:48:03 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ne.jpg" length="31036" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ne.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Tiani appoints Aboubacar Issaka Oumarou to lead Niger’s national police</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/ne/tiani-appoints-aboubacar-issaka-oumarou-to-lead-niger-s-4a335d/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/ne/tiani-appoints-aboubacar-issaka-oumarou-to-lead-niger-s-4a335d/</guid><category>Niger</category><description>The former head of the country’s narcotics-trafficking office was named police director general by a decree signed on 13 November.</description><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 10:16:21 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ne.jpg" length="31036" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ne.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Niger orders Mahamid Arabs to leave by 31 December</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/ne/niger-orders-mahamid-arabs-to-leave-by-31-december-2d66a4/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/ne/niger-orders-mahamid-arabs-to-leave-by-31-december-2d66a4/</guid><category>Niger</category><description>Several thousand members of the community, many settled in the south-east for decades, have been told to leave the country by the end of 2026.</description><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 03:39:13 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/ne/niger-orders-mahamid-arabs-to-leave-by-31-december-2d66a4/share.jpg" length="41108" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/ne/niger-orders-mahamid-arabs-to-leave-by-31-december-2d66a4/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
